A Simple Father-Daughter Conversation at the Zoo

Daughter: Daddy, where are we going today?
Father: We are going to the zoo!

Daughter: Yay! I love the zoo. Look! I see a lion.
Father: Yes, and the lion is roaring!

Daughter: Wow! It is so loud. Oh, I see an elephant.
Father: That’s right. The elephant has a long trunk.

Daughter: And there’s a turtle! It is moving so slowly.
Father: Yes, turtles are slow animals.

Daughter: Look at the rabbit! It has soft fur.
Father: Yes, rabbits are very soft and cute.

Daughter: Daddy, is that a monkey?
Father: No, that is a gorilla. The gorilla is eating a banana.

Daughter: Haha! He looks funny. I love the zoo!
Father: I’m glad you enjoy it! Let’s see more animals.

